    return 'fail'\n        return 'pass'\n    \n    # initial set is all items, but we work with a sorted list for determinism\n    C = sorted(items)\n    tests = 0\n    n = 2\n    while True:\n        # partition C into n subsets\n        k = len(C)\n        part_size = k // n\n        remainder = k % n\n        parts = []\n        idx = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            size = part_size + (1 if i < remainder else 0)\n            part = set(C[idx:idx+size])\n            idx += size\n            parts.append(part)\n        # test each part\n        found_fail = False\n        for part in parts:\n            tests += 1\n            res = test(part)\n            if res == 'fail':\n                C = sorted(part)\n                n = 2\n                found_fail = True\n                break\n        if found_fail:\n            continue\n        # test complements\n        C_set = set(C)\n        for part in parts:\n            complement = C_set - part\n            tests += 1\n            res = test(complement)\n            if res == 'fail':\n                C = sorted(complement)\n                n = max(n-1, 2)\n                found_fail = True\n                break\n        if found_fail:\n            continue\n        if n >= k:\n            break\n        n = min(n*2, k)\n    minimal_failure = C\n    outcome = 'failure'  # because we started with failing set and only reduced while maintaining failure\n    return {\n        'minimal_failure': minimal_failure,\n        'outcome': outcome,\n        'tests': tests\n    }\n```\n\nThis should work for the given cases. However, we must consider that the initial set may not fail? But the problem implies it does, because required_failure_items are all in items. So okay.\n\nAlso, we need to handle case where unresolved_without is present but not subset of full set? In the fixture, unresolved_without are always within items, so fine.\n\nNow, we need to produce the JSON with the code string. We'll escape backsla